  body: "# Joint beneficial ownership of capital\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation; unreviewed.
    No entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured guidance describes beneficial ownership
    through a beneficial interest and joint beneficial ownership where more than one person has that interest
    in the same capital.\n\n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 84072, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a5e38bb8b7e4fa537e693d5/dmg-ch84.pdf#page=8)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `f5c610b29bdb81e11736409b7f33ccf7917a4d8945f2821802801073e0d753ee`.\n\
    \nThe definition does not identify owners, shares, valuation or disregard entitlement in an individual
    case.\n\nThe capture date, the publication page's update date and a date stated in the guidance have
    different meanings. Linked legislation and memos need their own provision, version and applicability
    review.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/beneficial-ownership
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The paragraph directly relates joint ownership to beneficial interests in the same
      capital; it does not equate legal title with beneficial ownership.
    evidence:
    - page: page/84/0008
      quote: "84072 People are beneficial owners of capital if they have a beneficial interest in it.
        A person is the joint\nbeneficial owner of capital if more than one person has a beneficial interest
        in the same capital."
      locator: DMG 84072
